{
 "version": 1,
 "rule": "events/page",
 "cacheControl": "private, no-cache",
 "_doc": "GET /api/events in pages (#110). limit (1..2000) or page selects the paged form; without both the route answers the legacy array (streamed, Deprecation: true). valid pages decode and invalid ones are refused for the reason given; items are the legacy items exactly. requests run against a server where the caller has 5 events in $ws (so limit=2 has 3 pages), 1 in $otherWs and another user owns $bobWs; $next is the next token of the caller's first page with limit=2&workspace=$ws. error is the JSON code of {error, message}; text is the plain-text body (without its newline). readerAccepts marks an answer the server never sends but a reader must still follow: a page saved by the web service worker loses its lookup events, so a saved page can be empty with more true. budget.maxPageBytes counts the encoded bytes of the items alone (the page envelope and the commas between items are not counted), as in the pull. Tokens are opaque: only the e1. prefix is a contract. Decoded by server/internal/api/contract_events_page_test.go and apps/web/src/lib/events/eventPages.test.ts. cacheControl is the Cache-Control of every paged answer (private, no-cache: never kept by a shared cache, revalidated, and saved by the web service worker for offline study, which skips answers that say no-store).",
 "budget": {
  "maxLimit": 2000,
  "maxPageBytes": 4194304,
  "tokenPrefix": "e1.",
  "itemKeys": [
   "id",
   "userId",
   "workspaceId",
   "device",
   "ts",
   "type",
   "payload"
  ]
 },
